  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Cubs In Five** (2 other sources): Uploader says Cubs In Five was not actually played; the band did a Birthday Party cover, The Friend Catcher, instead [1][2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Age of Kings**: rare: 8 archived performances [4]\n- **Family Happiness**: rare: 7 archived performances [4]\n- **Outer Scorpion Squadron**: rare: 8 archived performances [4]\n- **Song for Dana Plato**: rare: 6 archived performances [4]\n- **Seeing Daylight**: rare: 13 archived performances [4]\n- **Home Again Garden Grove**: mythic rare: 2 archived performances [4]\n- **Plain**: rare: 3 archived performances [4]\n- **Cubs In Five**: back after 46 archived shows (1283 days) [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mountaingoats2011-04-05.ca14.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 20 songs; 79 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]\n- **mountaingoats2011-04-05.ca14.flac24**: source not stated; 20 songs; 79 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- A Silkworm cover was played with Tim Midgett taking the vocals [1]\n- A Silkworm cover was played with Tim Midgett taking the vocals [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mountaingoats2011-04-05.ca14.flac16**: taped by Brian Emerick; transferred by Brian Emerick; source: CA-14 Cards > CA-9100 Pre-amp > Edirol R-09HR 24-bit 48K > SDHC [1]. Also: Notes were compiled on 6 April 2011 by someone with the email name brian.emerick [1]\n- **mountaingoats2011-04-05.ca14.flac24**: taped by Brian Emerick; transferred by Brian Emerick; source: CA-14 Cards > CA-9100 Pre-amp > Edirol R-09HR 24-bit 48K > SDHC [2]. Also: This is a 24-bit transfer; it must be converted to 16-bit or MP3 before burning to CD [2]",
